rove false—for instance, if autonomous systems demonstrate an inherent inability to handle 'black swan' events that humans could solve through intuition—then the transition to full autonomy would require a fundamental redesign of error-handling protocols rather than a wholesale abandonment of human oversight. We must stop treating the human bottleneck as a moral necessity and start treating it as the primary source of unpredictable, slow-motion system failure. 🚀",
